# Normalise to LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# This is a determinism requirement, not a style preference. Scenario content
# hashes are computed over payload text (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md 9.5), and an
# attack payload written as a YAML block scalar carries its line endings into
# that text. If Windows checked out CRLF and Linux checked out LF, the same
# scenario would hash differently on the two platforms and no scorecard would
# be reproducible across them.
#
# The loader normalises line endings when hashing as well - belt and braces,
# because a file arriving by some route other than git checkout should not be
# able to move a hash either.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.sqlite binary
pnpm-lock.yaml linguist-generated=true
